## Codebase Patterns
- Test repos must set `user.name` and `user.email` in their own git config; the test harness hides the global config
- `initTempRepo()` in worktree tests creates a temp repo with an initial commit; use `realpathSync` on the dir when worktree paths will be compared
- Worktree path is `<repoRoot>/../<repoName>.<prefix><num>-<slug>` -- now computed by the shared `ticketWorktreePath` helper
- `enqueue` serializes all worktree and branch mutations; new worktree operations must go through it
- Build with `npm run build` before running tests when `src/` changed; tests run against `dist/`
- Run a single test suite: `npx esbuild test/<name>.test.ts --format=esm --bundle --packages=external --outdir=dist/test --sourcemap && node dist/test/<name>.test.js`
- When a test uses `initTempGitRepo({ templateDir })` and later does `git checkout main`, add `git branch -M main` right after init -- the test harness hides global config, so the default branch is 'master', not 'main'
