  - `addWorktreeForBranchNow` handles stale worktree cleanup the same way `addWorktreeNow` does -- both prune and force-remove existing paths
  - `isAncestor` works from any cwd that is inside the repo (including a worktree), so checking base ancestry after checkout works from the worktree path
  - The `git merge --abort` path is needed even though the test suite's merge conflicts are simple -- real conflicts may be partial merges that leave index state
