## 2026-11-20 - US-006
- Verified all provider-error ticket outcome code was already implemented in prior stories' uncommitted changes:
  - `TicketOutcome` has `{ kind:'provider-error' }` and `{ kind:'skipped' }` variants
  - `runTicketAttempt` returns `provider-error` after `spawnAgent` when `providerError` is set, removing the worktree but keeping the branch
  - `runTicketAttempts` returns `stop:true` for `provider-error`, preventing retries
  - `attemptEntry` records `provider-error` with outcome `'error'` and the message; `skipped` returns null (never recorded)
  - `runWavesIsolated` wave outcome loop adds `provider-error` and `skipped` to `failedKeys` without touching ticket status or progress.md
- Fixed integration test 'a provider error keeps the ticket branch': added `git branch -M main` after `initTempGitRepo({ templateDir })` so `git checkout main` works under the test harness (which hides global git config, making the default branch 'master')
- Files changed: `test/integration.test.ts`, `specs/prd.json`, `progress.log`
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - When a test uses `initTempGitRepo({ templateDir })` and needs to switch back to the base branch by name, use `git branch -M main` immediately after init -- the `cliGitRepo()` helper already does this, but direct callers must do it themselves
  - The test harness (`scripts/test.sh`) sets `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1` and a custom `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL`, so `init.defaultBranch` is unset and git falls back to its compiled-in default ('master' on git 2.49.0)
