## 2026-11-20 - US-007
- Implemented provider-error run stop in `runWavesIsolated`:
  - Added `stop:{ reason:string|null }` local variable
  - Pool callback returns `{ kind:'skipped' }` when `stop.reason` is set
  - After `runTicketAttempts` returns a `provider-error`, `stop.reason` is set to a message naming `opts.model` and the error
  - Already-finished tickets in the same wave still merge normally
  - After the wave outcome loop, `stop.reason` is logged and the wave loop breaks
  - End-of-run review pass is skipped when `stop.reason` is set
- Added integration test 'a provider error stops the run': two independent ready tickets, `--concurrency 1 --retries 2`, fake pi delegating to `mock-agent-pi-error.js`; asserts exit code 1, exactly one invocation in `FAKE_PI_RECORD_DIR`, and both tickets still `ready-for-agent`
- Files changed: `src/orchestrator.ts`, `test/integration.test.ts`, `specs/prd.json`, `progress.log`
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - `stop.reason` must be set inside the pool callback (after `runTicketAttempts` returns), not in the post-pool outcome loop -- the pool runs items sequentially with `concurrency 1`, so setting it after the pool finishes is too late to prevent the second ticket from running
  - The `runPool` worker loop checks `stop.reason` before each item, so a stop from one ticket prevents the next ticket in the same wave from starting, but already-running tickets finish normally
